# Backend request: expose variation cover images

Expose each product variation's configured cover image in the public catalog responses:

- `GET /api/products`
- `GET /api/products/{id}`, including numeric IDs, product codes, and supported aliases.

## Response contract

Add `coverImageUrl: string | null` to every object in `variants`:

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "code": "ic",
  "image": "https://example.com/product-cover.jpg",
  "images": ["https://example.com/product-cover.jpg"],
  "variants": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "style": "FULL",
      "label": "Full",
      "active": true,
      "coverImageUrl": "https://example.com/ic-full-cover.jpg",
      "packages": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "style": "BORDER",
      "label": "Border (Polaroid)",
      "active": true,
      "coverImageUrl": "https://example.com/ic-border-cover.jpg",
      "packages": []
    }
  ]
}
```

This example shows relevant fields only; preserve all existing response fields and package data.

## Requirements

- Read the cover configured for the specific variation in the admin catalog.
- Return an absolute HTTPS URL accessible by the storefront without admin authentication.
- Always include `coverImageUrl`; use `null` when no variation cover is configured.
- Preserve existing product-level `image` and `images` fields.
- Return the same variation cover URL in list and detail responses.
- Reflect admin cover updates and removals in subsequent public responses.
- Preserve existing alias filtering behavior.

## Verification

1. Configure different cover images for IC FULL and BORDER.
2. Confirm the list and detail endpoints return the respective URLs.
3. Check numeric-ID, product-code, and supported alias detail requests.
4. Verify a variation without a cover returns `coverImageUrl: null`.
5. Change and remove a cover, confirming the public responses reflect each action.
6. Verify the image URLs can be loaded without admin authentication.

## Frontend follow-up

Once deployed, the frontend must add this field to `ProductVariant` and preserve it in `normalizeVariants` in `src/lib/product-pricing.ts`. The selected variation's cover can then be displayed, falling back to the parent product image when null. Current catalog cards and the product gallery use parent product images.

## Observed baseline

On 2026-10-18, the deployed backend at `https://polaroid-glossy-backend.fly.dev` returned only `id`, `style`, `label`, `active`, and `packages` for all 11 variants in `GET /api/products`. The IC detail response also omitted variation image fields.
